          "id": "india-wpi-october-2026-11-16",
          "headline": "Wholesale inflation climbs to 12.29% in October as fuel and power costs jump",
          "summary": "Wholesale (WPI) inflation rose to 12.29% in October from 11.39% in September, provisional Commerce Ministry data show. Fuel and power prices were up 32.84% from a year ago, against 25.85% in September. Food inflation eased slightly to 8.58%, and manufactured goods to 9.54% from 9.76%.",
          "why_it_matters": "With retail inflation already above the RBI's 6% ceiling, rising factory-gate prices make another rate hike more likely.",
