          "headline": "Tata Motors PV falls about 9% as JLR cuts its profit and cash outlook",
          "summary": "Tata Motors Passenger Vehicles shares fell as much as 8.6% to Rs 262.40 after Jaguar Land Rover cut its FY27 EBIT margin guidance to 2-3% from 4%. JLR now expects about £1.25 billion of cash outflow this year instead of breakeven, citing weak China sales and restructuring costs. The company posted a September-quarter loss of about Rs 5,500 crore after one-off charges of Rs 6,738 crore.",
